rpshow NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

* Noteworthy changes in release 0.2 (????-??-??) [?]

** New features

  Markdown files (.md, .markdown, .mdown, .mkd, .mkdn, .mdwn) are
  rendered with Python's rich module on the remote host, like
  "python3 -m rich.markdown -c -p FILE", and shown in less -R.
  Without rich the source is shown, with a note.  The new option
  --raw (-r) shows the source on purpose.

  PDF files (.pdf in any case, or any file starting with "%PDF-") are
  shown fullscreen in zathura on the remote host, recoloured dark with
  the colours from the local zathurarc; a right click closes them.
  The new option --light (-l) shows the pages in their own colours,
  and --raw (-r) shows a PDF as text in less.  Without zathura the PDF
  is shown as text, with a note.

** Bug fixes

  lesspipe works again on remote hosts whose less knows
  LESSSECURE_ALLOW: secure mode had turned it off, so compressed files
  and PDFs were shown as raw bytes.

* Noteworthy changes in release 0.1 (2026-10-05)

** New features

  First release.  rpshow FILE copies FILE over ssh to a Raspberry Pi and
  shows it in less, in a fullscreen alacritty window on the Pi's screen.
  A right click closes the window.  Options: --host, --display, --wait,
  --verbose, --help, --version.

  The remote host needs alacritty 0.13 or later: the window settings are
  passed as TOML overrides.  If alacritty reports that it ignored one of
  them, rpshow closes the window and exits with status 1, since such a
  window may not close on a right click.
